A||N||5||Haze_Performance||120 Speedo Info needed..||||4||
Z||000000||Haze_Performance||07-31-2001||04:53 PM||||I want to put a 120 speedo cluster in my '84. How do I recalibrate the tach? I know everything else is plug & play.<P>TFTI<BR><I><B>Haze</I></B>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/indyclick.gif">   <BR></A><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Click above to visit my website.</B></FONT></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 07-31-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000001||Leadfoot||07-31-2001||05:03 PM||||Haze, you shouldn't have to recalibrate if you swapped, but it is a good thing to do.  I found some info. on how to do it at this site.<BR> <A HREF="http://home.t-online.de/home/O_Scholz/fieroidx.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.t-online.de/home/O_Scholz/fieroidx.html</A> <P>All I did was the turn ignition to run and set the needle to zero.  Worked pretty good.<BR>Boy, sure sounds like you are doing the same upgrades I did, i.e. sail panels, gauges.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||07-31-2001||05:19 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Leadfoot:<BR><B>Haze, you shouldn't have to recalibrate if you swapped, but it is a good thing to do.  I found some info. on how to do it at this site.<BR> <A HREF="http://home.t-online.de/home/O_Scholz/fieroidx.html" TARGET=_blank>http://home.t-online.de/home/O_Scholz/fieroidx.html</A> <P>All I did was the turn ignition to run and set the needle to zero.  Worked pretty good.<BR>Boy, sure sounds like you are doing the same upgrades I did, i.e. sail panels, gauges.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Hey Lead,<BR>  The tach will read differently form V6 to 4. I had a 120 in my '85 for awhile & it bugged me. But not I'm going to try the '84. Its a 4-speed. It will really drive me nuts if I keep seeing the needle peg out every time I shift.   Thanks for the link.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <BR><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/indyclick.gif">  <BR></A><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Click above to visit my website.</B></FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000003||KRMFiero||07-31-2001||06:03 PM||||how about re calibrating from 6 cyl to 8 for my caddy conversion...||||reg||1
Z||000004||84 2in1||08-01-2001||02:59 PM||||how about a 4 to a 8 for a caddy conversion?-B-||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||08-01-2001||04:56 PM||||Find the 2554339 chip, find pins 5 and 8. Cut the traces to these pins and install a 50k trimmer pot from radio Shack. Adjust the pot so the tach reads correctly. If the tach jumps at all, find the capactor that was also across pins 5 and 8 (when you cut the traces, you disconnected this cap) and solder it back across pins 5 and 8.<P>This mod allows you to change the full scale of the tach. Works for speedo's too. Now it will work on Allison V16's if necessary. ||||reg||1
